Tuikio: local play only, and no SQLite.

- Upstream's -serve flag starts an SSH server (wish) that serves the game to others over the
  network; a phone game has no business listening for connections, so that mode and its imports
  are left out.
- The game history behind the total score was kept in SQLite through the pure-Go modernc.org/sqlite
  driver, about 4 MB of every binary for three queries. store/file.go keeps the same history in a
  small JSON file ($HOME/.local/share/clidle/clidle.json) with the same three operations and the
  same score (10 x (11 - guesses) per won game). The game itself is unchanged.

